# Accessibility & Field Usability (SR-App)

Detailed reference: `docs/steering/technical/accessibility.md`.

**Hard rules**
- **Semantic HTML + ARIA** where needed; labeled forms; real buttons/links for interactive elements.
- **Large touch targets** (min ~44px) for primary field actions; generous spacing to avoid mis-taps.
- **Keyboard operable** + focus-visible on admin surfaces.
- **WCAG AA contrast**; **never rely on color alone** (job status + text label; location freshness + text).
- **Readable outdoors** — high-contrast defaults; avoid low-contrast gray-on-white for critical info.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; don't gate critical actions behind hover.
- Error/validation messages are text, associated with fields (not color-only).

**Guidance:** lean on shadcn/ui accessible primitives; test the field flow on a real small viewport; verify one-handed reach of the action bar.

**DoD:** semantic/labeled controls; AA contrast; field-sized touch targets; state conveyed with text not just color; field action bar reachable one-handed.
